PR182_REVIEW_FINDING_V1_FOLLOWUP

The first finding fix exposed three hosted contract guards that still encoded the superseded reviewer-first wording. CI also made the remaining prose drift obvious: the benchmark section heading had been deferred, but one sentence still called reviewer the "first production/evaluation integration".

Disposition: same confirmed failure class -> closed repository-wide.

Follow-up fix on current HEAD 7cfc35f5bdfa2e2cf31858c9f27846b837958de1:
- remove the remaining "first production/evaluation integration" reviewer wording;
- update `test_automatic_reviewer_research_contract.py` to require the deferred specialist rung;
- update `test_benchmark_evaluation_strategy_contract.py` to require Core-v1 as immediate priority and reviewer/session expansion as deferred;
- rename the reviewer benchmark contract test to describe a specific-but-deferred application;
- keep the dedicated documentation-consistency negative guard against reintroducing reviewer-first priority/rung phrases.

No production/runtime/authority behavior changed. The previous review remains stale; rerun hosted checks before the fresh exact-head semantic review.
